WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.949
the indispensable nation is just a happy

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:03.179
mythology we like to tell ourselves

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:05.220
to justify policies that we happen to

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.860
already do many times for other reasons

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.380
Hi I'm Nick Gillespie with Reason TV

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.930
today we're talking with Trevor Thrall

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.990
he is a senior fellow who covers defense and

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.940
security issues at the Cato Institute

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.880
he's also a professor at George Mason University

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.480
Trevor thanks for talking to us

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.140
Nick great to be here

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.680
you have written a fair amount about

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.560
the Trump Doctrine

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.760
obviously this is a bit you

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.360
you know it's constantly being

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.040
revised it's like a google doc that

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.360
probably has 50 different people

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.070
you know monkeying with it

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.289
how do you see like how can we

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:45.449
meaningfully talk about Donald Trump's

00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:47.370
foreign policy and what it's likely to go towards

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.440
yeah great question

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.350
I think it's he's so inconsistent it is a

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.670
little tricky putting your finger right

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.190
on it but i think we now know enough

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.469
that we can identify at least three big

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:00.750
pillars to start talking about it

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.380
the first is embodied in that

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.740
America first tag line and that is a sort of

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.240
über American nationalism and what I

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.930
think that really means at heart is

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:13.229
that Trump is indifferent to really the

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:15.150
the project of the post-world war two

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.640
American foreign policy regime which was

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.200
building and maintaining a

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.680
liberal international order

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.680
he doesn't care about the liberal international order

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.140
he cares only about America's

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.120
NATO other allies

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.540
providing global public goods like

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.280
safe passage in the ocean he doesn't think

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.880
or care much about any of those things

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.120
so that's number one

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.000
number two is

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.110
on the other hand you might think that made him

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.909
sort of a dove or something but

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:40.110
I think the second thing is that he's

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:43.680
actually hawkish he's actually very

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.990
I don't think he wants to intervene very

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.340
often doesn't care too much about the rest of the world

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.320
but when he does I think he wants

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.790
to bring the hammer and so if you listen

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.320
to his words about ISIS

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.620
I'm going to bomb the shit out of them

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.320
eradicating radical Islam and stuff like that so I think

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.670
he's you know he's not interested in the

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.039
general project of liberal internationalism

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.110
but when it comes to push and shove

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.490
I think he kinda has a zero-sum way of

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.700
thinking about the world we're gonna win

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.840
and we're going to beat people up hard to do it

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.320
and I think the third piece that

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.090
we've seen very clearly and also kind of

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.490
stems from the America first tagline

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.560
is his economic nationalism which is

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.750
again very a big break from the

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.730
Republican party for sure but even from

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.220
Democratic elites so you know

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.280
trade war with China is on the horizon

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:26.740
that sort of stuff

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.420
tariffs and you know

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.420
no support really that I can see for free trade

